// ===========================================================================================
// COSMOS-SDK L1 EXPLOIT-PoC HARNESS — consensus-halt / nondeterminism   [the highest-value shape]
// ---
// WHY THIS EXISTS
//   The dominant, highest-severity L1 critical is a CONSENSUS HALT — a nondeterministic state
//   path (all nodes must compute the same AppHash) or an unrecovered panic in BeginBlock/EndBlock
//   (every validator runs the identical block, so ONE panic halts the WHOLE chain). Neither has a
//   static net (docs/cosmos-notes.md §4). This template proves them two ways:
//     A) NONDETERMINISM: execute the suspect path TWICE and show the two runs produce different
//        state bytes / AppHash. Divergence = the halt.  (checklist §1, PC §1)
//     B) HALT-BY-PANIC: actually invoke BeginBlock/EndBlock (or an ante/keeper path) on
//        attacker-planted state and show it PANICS.       (checklist §6/§4.2, PC §6)
//
// COVERAGE CANARY (strict for this class — the failure is silent until production)
//   A) The suspect path MUST actually run on BOTH runs, and you compare REAL post-state bytes /
//      AppHash, not a value the harness set. A single run, or comparing a harness counter, proves
//      nothing.
//   B) require.Panics MUST wrap the REAL BeginBlock/EndBlock call reaching the target — assert the
//      panic comes from the target path (recover + inspect message/stack), not from the harness.
//   A green determinism test that never executed the nondeterministic branch is a lie (repo rule).
//
// FIRST: does the app already ship TestAppStateDeterminism? If so, RUN IT — it fuzzes random msg
//   sequences and asserts identical AppHash across repeated runs of the same seed
//   (`make test-sim-nondeterminism`). It catches a class of §1 bugs for free. This template is for
//   when you have a SPECIFIC suspect path the sim's random ops won't reliably hit, or the in-scope
//   module isn't wired into the app's simapp.
//
// SETUP
//   1) Match the target's go.mod (cosmos-sdk / cometbft). The app constructor + FinalizeBlock/
//      Commit API differ across SDK v0.47 (BeginBlock/EndBlock/DeliverTx) vs v0.50+ (FinalizeBlock).
//      Use the TARGET app's own test helper (`app.Setup`, `simapp.New…`) — do not reinvent wiring.
//   2) Copy into the target's app/ package (or a package that can import the whole app).
//   3) Run:  go test ./app -run 'TestPoC_(Nondeterminism|HaltByPanic)' -v
// ===========================================================================================

